<title>USA: Ford October U.S. vehicle sales rise.</title>
<headline>Ford October U.S. vehicle sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co</p>
<p>			Oct 1-31, 1996     Oct 1-31, 1995 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Domestic Car	   140,806	   139,609	     -2.9</p>
<p> Domestic Truck	 191,399	   170,234	     +8.3</p>
<p> Import Car		 2,385	     3,826	    -40.0</p>
<p> Import Truck		   0		   0	     N.A.</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-Oct 31, 1996 Jan 1-Oct 31, 1995 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Domestic Car	 1,461,348	 1,480,280	     -2.0</p>
<p> Domestic Truck     1,758,000	 1,698,984	     +2.7</p>
<p> Import Car		34,107	    53,891	    -37.2</p>
<p> Import Truck		   0		   0	     N.A.</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 27 in latest month vs 26, 258 for year to date vs 256 in year ago.</p>
<p>Note: Table does not include sales of heavy trucks of 3,291 and 3,913 in October '96 and '95, and 38,778 and 48,596 in '96 and '95 year-to-date periods.</p>
<p>Including heavy truck sales, Ford total October sales rose 2.5 pct on daily selling basis.</p>
</text>
